        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-14 02:28:54.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-930 doc: package man pages by directory, not by list",
        "message": "LU-930 doc: package man pages by directory, not by list\n\nUse wildcards to generate the list pages under Documentation/man*/\ninstead of requiring that every new manpage explicitly add itself\nto the list of files packaged. That is either error-prone and omits\nthe new page from the package, or causes patches to have needless\nconflicts in context, a loss either way.\n\nThe man4/ pages gain a new Makefile.am, since they were only added\nin this release, and it was deferred exactly to avoid contention.\n\nFor man4/ and man8/, wildcards and a short list of filenames are\nused to filter out server commands or parameters.  If forgotten, at\nworst an extra page is installed on the client.  Checkpatch.pl will\nwarn on patches changing Makefile.am, since explicit updates should\nonly be needed rarely when a new server exception is added.\n\nThe current explicit list of manpages is left in-place temporarily\nfor man1, man3, and man8 to avoid conflict with patches already in\nflight, but are no longer used for packaging.  They can be removed\nin 2.18.53 when older patches need to be refreshed anyway.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ia8afaf6502d5cdd47801824c6c6b3b5d969ca77a\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
